  "text": "Reviewing changes from branch 107-migrate-specify-command-to-script:\n\n### New Files Being Added:\n1. `skills/cc-track-tools/scripts/specify.ts` - Main script for spec infrastructure creation\n2. `skills/cc-track-tools/scripts/specify.test.ts` - Tests for the specify script\n3. Modified: `commands/specify.md` - Command documentation\n4. Modified: `skills/cc-track-tools/SKILL.md` - Skill documentation\n5. Modified: `skills/cc-track-tools/lib/git-helpers.ts` - Added `branchExists()` method\n\n### Key Finding:\nThe new `specify.ts` script REUSES existing library functions from the cc-track codebase:\n- Uses `spec-helpers.ts` functions: getNextTaskId, generateFeatureName, createSpecDirectory, createMetadata\n- Uses `git-helpers.ts` methods: createTaskBranch, getCurrentBranch, branchExists\n- Uses `github-helpers.ts` methods: createGitHubIssue\n- Uses `config.ts`: isGitHubIntegrationEnabled\n- Uses `logger.ts`: createLogger\n\nNO DUPLICATE IMPLEMENTATION - The script properly composes existing utilities rather than reimplementing them.\n\nThe new `branchExists()` method in git-helpers.ts appears to be NEW functionality (not a duplicate) as no prior implementation was found.",
  "sections": [
    "Project Notes",
    "Duplication Analysis Summary"
